**Motion findings:** motion instants — stem removal ≈1000–2000 ms · hand release ≈2000–2500 ms · press descent ≈3000–4000 ms (mid at F-3500) · reveal between 4000–4500 ms (the cutter's lift/flip is a stop-motion jump inside this interval; the slab is simply THERE at 4500) · gather ≈5000–6000 ms · bowl addition by 7000 ms. Holds — the stem-on state is evidenced AT CP1 (source 40.0 s) only; seg-rel 0–1000 ms is the prior episode (CP0), so any opening stem-on hold in the build is an ALLOCATION choice, not a census hold (jev-observe-exit charge 2, applied) · solo cushion ≈2500–3000 ms · slab on cutter ≈4500–5000 ms · final bowl state at 7000 ms. What changes between states: stem star present→absent (CP1→CP2) · hands present→absent (CP2→CP3) · grid absent→covering (CP3→CP4, the occlusion that carries the swap) · cushion→red-dice slab under the lifted cutter (CP4→F-4500) · slab on cutter→dice in hands→dice in bowl (CP5→CP7). The grid in CP4/F-4500 reads ≈7 columns × 6 rows of square cells with wooden side handles.
**Sub-beats:** SB-A stem-on presentation · SB-B stem removal (pins retained) · SB-C solo hold · SB-D grid descent + press (squash under occlusion) · SB-E occlusion hold (swap rides here) · SB-F lift + dice-slab reveal · SB-G slab hold · SB-H gather · SB-I bowl addition + final hold.

### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Subject — cushion centre/radius, fill + dark fill, seam colour + seam count, pin set (per-pin offset + colour index), stem star (point list, fill, scale).
2. Tool — grid columns/rows, cell size, frame/handle geometry + colours, press travel distance, squash factor at press bottom, occluder opacity max (the swap's cover at press bottom).
3. Output — cube columns/rows/layers (slab footprint), cube size, cube fill/edge, pip style (dice/plain), pip colour/radius, per-cube reveal stagger, seeded RNG seed for pip counts.
4. Bowl — bowl centre/radius, bowl + inner (green flesh) colours, prior-contents count (white cubes already in bowl), final cube slot arrangement (derived from cube index).
5. Labels — input label text, tool label text, output label text, label font sizes + family, label positions (derived from subject/grid/bowl centres).
6. Timing — stem-off start/duration, settle duration, press duration, press-hold duration, lift duration, slab-hold duration, gather duration, final hold; phase starts DERIVED sequentially (never independent keys — a timing swap cannot orphan a later phase).
7. Palette — board, board-dark, cushion, cushion-dark, seam, stem, pin colours, grid metal/dark, handle, cube, cube edge, pip, bowl, bowl-inner, prior-cube, ink/label colours.
8. Easing — per-phase easing names.

### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
- A1 §2 typography precedent: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; text is DOM/SVG label text rendered from CONFIG strings.
- A5 Owner Cures 1–2: NOT APPLICABLE as particle cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogue carried: phase exclusivity by construction — phases are sequential-derived and the input/output identities never coexist visibly (output appears only after the swap instant inside occlusion; Owner Cure 2's exclusivity in schedule form).
- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool.
- A9.1 plate construction: NOT APPLICABLE — no moving background plate; the board is still. The moving GRID is the tool, priced in §2.1 as tool geometry, not a plate.
- Family: Packet #13 substitution siblings — T232 (dice literalization, Wave 36 NO VERDICT, receipt-form cures: CONFIG expressions on fixed census rows · a MOVED evaluation instant at a census-anchored probe · key-binding receipts) and T227 (Wave 36 NO VERDICT, phase-relative receipt cures). **Sibling cures carried binding into §2.3/§2.4:** every census probe carries its CONFIG expression · the timing swap receipt shows a moved instant at a census-anchored probe (not only at phase probes) · every CONFIG key incl. `pipStyle` is bound in the renderer with a swapped-value receipt · raw phase value and eased result printed separately.

## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 400 · subjectCx 300 · subjectCy 188 · subjectR 80 · seamCount 6 · pinRadiusPx 6 · stemScale 1 · gridCols 7 · gridRows 6 · cellPx 36 · handleW 56 · handleHPx 22 · pressTravelPx 170 · pressSquash 0.38 · occluderMax 1.0 · cubeCols 3 · cubeRows 3 · cubeLayers 2 · cubeGapPx 2 · layerOffsetPx 6 · revealStaggerFraction 0.6 · pipStyle "dice" · pipRadiusPx 4.5 · rngSeed 233 · bowlCx 472 · bowlCy 296 · bowlR 96 · bowlSlotInset 0.62 · priorCubes 7 · labelFontPx 21 · toolLabelFontPx 16 · inputLabelDy 118 · outputLabelDy 118 · fontFamily "Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif" · inputLabel "TOMATO PINCUSHION" · toolLabel "GRID PRESS" · outputLabel "DICED TOMATO" · tStemOffMs 0 · stemOffDurMs 1000 · settleDurMs 1000 · pressDurMs 1000 · pressHoldMs 250 · liftDurMs 250 · slabHoldMs 750 · gatherDurMs 1750 · holdMs 1000 · easeStem/easePress/easeLift/easeGather "easeInOut" · easeSettle "linear" (the settle phase is a STATIC hold — no motion to ease; the key exists so every phase names its rule, jev-plan-exit cure) · palette {board #8a6844, boardDark #6f5233, cushion #d8262c, cushionDark #a8161c, seam #2e5d3a, stem #2e7d46, pinColors [#f5eeda,#e8a0a8,#c1272d,#f2c14e], grid #5a6068, gridDark #363b42, handle #b08d5f, cube #e0232e, cubeEdge #8f1218, pip #ffffff, bowl #4a4a48, bowlInner #79c142, priorCube #f2f2f2, labelInk #ffffff, labelHalo #3a2a18}`.
Nested: `pins[12]` — `{dx, dy, ci}` (offsets in subject radii, colour index into palette.pinColors): (-0.55,-0.42,0) (-0.28,-0.62,1) (0.02,-0.70,2) (0.34,-0.58,3) (0.58,-0.30,0) (-0.62,-0.02,1) (-0.30,-0.18,3) (0.05,-0.28,0) (0.38,-0.08,1) (-0.48,0.28,2) (-0.12,0.10,3) (0.30,0.30,0). `stemStar[10]` — normalized star points [[0,-0.62],[0.16,-0.20],[0.58,-0.30],[0.28,0.06],[0.44,0.48],[0,0.26],[-0.44,0.48],[-0.28,0.06],[-0.58,-0.30],[-0.16,-0.20]] (10 points, closed). Counts are DERIVED from the arrays (pins.length, stemStar.length printed by the harness), never restated as literals.
Derived (named, never stored): stemStart=tStemOffMs (=0) · stemEnd=stemStart+stemOffDurMs (=1000) · pressStart=stemEnd+settleDurMs (=2000) · pressEnd=pressStart+pressDurMs (=3000) · holdEnd=pressEnd+pressHoldMs (=3250) · liftEnd=holdEnd+liftDurMs (=3500) · gatherStart=liftEnd+slabHoldMs (=4250) · completeAtMs=gatherStart+gatherDurMs (=6000) · durationMs=completeAtMs+holdMs (=7000) · swapAtMs=pressEnd+pressHoldMs/2 (=3125) · cubePx = cellPx − cubeGapPx (=34; the slab footprint 3×34+2×2 = 106 px ≈ 3 grid cells = 108 px — the output footprint is TIED to the grid that forces it, codex-plan-review cure) · cubeTotal=cubeCols×cubeRows×cubeLayers (=18; count assertion: source-count 18 = built-count 18, harness-printed) · grid geometry from gridCx=subjectCx, gridCy=subjectCy, cols/rows/cellPx · cube slab origin centred on subject · per-cube reveal stagger = cubeIndex/(cubeTotal−1) × revealStaggerFraction × liftDurMs, each cube's own reveal completing by liftEnd (validated) · bowl slots derived per cube index (ring positions at bowlR × bowlSlotInset) · **occluder**: a tool-local OPAQUE cover rect inside the grid group (fill gridDark, opacity = occluderMax = 1.0 at press bottom) whose bounds cover the subject's full silhouette (coverW = gridCols×cellPx, coverH = gridRows×cellPx, centred on the subject) — at press bottom the changing silhouette is geometrically concealed, not merely dimmed (codex-plan-review cure); the cover lifts WITH the grid group, uncovering the armed cubes from the top during the lift. Before press bottom the cushion stays visible through the grid cells (continuous with CP4's fragments); its squash is continuous across the swap boundary (P11 checks coverage + composited visibility at swap−1, swap, swap+1). **Validation:** all durations >0 and finite; counts positive integers; pressSquash in (0,1); **occluderMax MUST equal 1** (a configuration below full opacity is rejected — P11's concealment guarantee holds for every accepted configuration, jev-plan-exit cure; the harness additionally asserts cover bounds ⊇ subject bounds at the default geometry AND at a subjectR × 1.2 variant); revealStaggerFraction in [0,1); a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered. Phase order is sequential by derivation — overlap is impossible by construction.

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG single-stage scene (chosen):** one SVG; board rect; bowl group (fades in for the final act); cushion group (circle + seam lines + pin circles + stem star polygon) with press squash (scaleY about its base); grid group (cell lines + frame + handles + occluder rect) translating Y by press/lift progress; cube group (per-cube rect + pip circles when pipStyle="dice") revealed staggered after the swap instant, then translated to bowl slots during gather; three CONFIG label texts. All geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Photographic/generated imagery — approaches the specimen; the technique is the tool-forced identity change, carried by geometry.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) CP0 prior-episode bowl tail (source 39–40 s) — outside this technique; the allocation discards it (departure table §2.3). (2) Hands — not built; the actions (stem lift, press, gather) are performed by the objects' own motion, the fleet's diagram form for performed-action techniques (T218 precedent). (3) The source's separate bowl SHOT (CP7 is a cut to the bowl) is compressed onto the single stage: the bowl fades in at gather and the cubes travel to it — a named single-stage departure, printed on the comparison's face via the allocation note in build-record. (4) Spare background pincushions (top-right dressing) — omitted as set dressing, not technique. (5) The source's reveal is an abrupt stop-motion jump (CP4→F-4500, no intermediate state in the census); the build's staggered reveal over liftDurMs is a deliberate replacement, named here as a fidelity departure (jev-plan-exit cure) — it is priced in §2.5 and the motion lens judges it with this naming on the record.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: **t=0 allocation** — build 0 ms = source 40.0 s (segment-relative 1000 ms); build instant = census seg-rel − 1000. Departure table: census CP0 (seg-rel 0, prior-episode bowl) has NO build counterpart (deferral §2.2 (1)); CP7's separate bowl shot is compressed per deferral (3) — its STATE (red cubes in bowl) is the build's final state, its shot boundary is not reproduced.
Assertions (CONFIG expression → evaluated instant; every receipt prints raw phase + eased result separately, full predicates over ALL pins/cubes; schedule AMENDED at §2b under codex-plan-review — stem completes by build 1000 per CP2, reveal completes by build 3500 per F-4500, CP5 at build 4000 is the slab HOLD):
- P0 stem start: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tStemOffMs)` → 0 ms: stemP 0, stemOpacity 1, pressP 0, cubeVisible 0.
- P1 stem mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tStemOffMs + CONFIG.stemOffDurMs/2)` → 500 ms: raw stemP 0.5, stemOpacity 0.5.
- P2 press start: `stateAt(CONFIG, stemEnd + CONFIG.settleDurMs)` → 2000 ms: stemOpacity 0, pressP 0, grid offset = −pressTravelPx.
- P3 press mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, pressStart + CONFIG.pressDurMs/2)` → 2500 ms: raw pressP 0.5, squash = 1−pressSquash×0.5.
- P4 press bottom (ZERO-STATE anchor for output, guards cmd 8): `stateAt(CONFIG, pressStart + CONFIG.pressDurMs)` → 3000 ms: pressP 1, occluderOpacity = occluderMax (1.0), cover bounds ⊇ subject bounds (geometry predicate printed), cubeVisible 0, inputOpacity 1.
- P5 swap instant: `stateAt(CONFIG, pressStart + CONFIG.pressDurMs + CONFIG.pressHoldMs/2)` → 3125 ms: inputOpacity 0, cubesArmed 1, cubeVisible 0 (armed ≠ visible — reveal rides the lift), occluderOpacity 1.
- P6 lift mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, holdEnd + CONFIG.liftDurMs/2)` → 3375 ms: liftP 0.5, cubeVisible ≥ 9 (top layer revealed).
- P7 reveal complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, holdEnd + CONFIG.liftDurMs)` → 3500 ms: cubeVisible = cubeTotal (18), every cube at slab position (full predicate), grid at rest, inputOpacity 0.
- P8 gather mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, gatherStart + CONFIG.gatherDurMs/2)` → 5125 ms: gatherP raw 0.5, bowlOpacity 0.5, every cube between slab and bowl slot.
- P9 complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs)` → 6000 ms: gatherP 1, bowlOpacity 1, every cube at its bowl slot.
- P10 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 500)` fully equal to P9 state — RAW FULL-STATE equality over the whole state object (every pin, cube, phase value), not a sampled predicate (T227 Cycle-040 cure form, carried per jev-observe-exit charge 1). durationMs = 7000.
- P11 swap boundary-jump: `stateAt(CONFIG, swapAtMs − 1)` vs `stateAt(CONFIG, swapAtMs)` vs `stateAt(CONFIG, swapAtMs + 1)` — the ONLY differing fields across the boundary are inputOpacity (1→0) and cubesArmed (0→1); squash, grid offset, and occluderOpacity are CONTINUOUS (equal at swap−1 and swap+1 within the phase's own progression) and occluderOpacity = 1 at all three instants, so the composited input visibility is 0 at the toggle (within-step equality + boundary-jump check, T227 cure form; coverage form per codex-plan-review). Zero-state fallback expression: at P4 the output predicate is `cubeVisible === 0` evaluated from the CONFIG expression `cubeTotal × revealP(3000)` with revealP printed raw (0) — an executable expression for the empty state, not a bare constant (T232 cure form).
- **Fixed census-instant probes (C*, build = seg-rel − 1000; F-4500 and CP5 are DISTINCT rows):** C@0 (CP1, source 40 stem-on) stemOpacity 1, pressP 0 · C@1000 (CP2, source 41 stem-off) stemOpacity 0 · C@1500 (F-2500, source 41.5 hand-release) stemOpacity 0 AND pressP 0 AND cushion at rest (the hand is a named omission — this row prices the settled-cushion analogue) · C@2000 (CP3, source 42 solo) pressP 0 AND stemOpacity 0 AND cubeVisible 0 · C@2500 (F-3500, source 42.5 press mid) state equal to P3 · C@3000 (CP4, source 43 press bottom) pressP 1 AND cubeVisible 0 (state equal to P4) · C@3500 (F-4500, source 43.5 reveal) cubeVisible 18 AND inputOpacity 0 (state equal to P7) · C@4000 (CP5, source 44 slab hold) cubeVisible 18 AND every cube at slab position AND gatherP 0 · C@4500 (F-5500, source 44.5 gather in hands) gatherP raw = 250/1750 ≈ 0.1429 AND at least one cube departed its slab position · C@5000 (CP6, source 45 gather continuing) gatherP raw = 750/1750 ≈ 0.4286 AND bowlOpacity > 0 · C@6000 (CP7, source 46 bowl) state equal to P9.

